==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|præsumptuous}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|presumptuous}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|presumptieus}}, {{m|fro|presumpcieus}}, {{m|fro|presumptuos}}, from {{der|en|la|praesumptuosus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɹəˈzʌmp.tjuː.əs/|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/pɹiˈzəmptʃuəs/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Going beyond what is [[right]], [[proper]], or [[appropriate]] because of an excess of [[self-confidence]] or [[arrogance]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|going beyond what is proper}} {{l|en|overconfident}}, {{l|en|foolhardy}}, {{l|en|rash}}, {{l|en|presuming}}, {{l|en|forward}}, {{l|en|arrogant}}, {{l|en|insolent}}, {{l|en|conceited}}
* See also: [[Thesaurus:arrogant]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|presumption}}
* {{l|en|presume}}

